	(text "/AGND_SENSE - the -IN sense run: U1 pin 3 to R5's bottom pad, tied to GND ONLY through R8"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 90.17 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "53edb8f4-ab44-4325-a2a1-883f1eaba998")
	)
	(text "J2 PIN 1 = +3V3  -  180 deg mis-mate shorts the host rail to its ground (unprotected)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 190.5 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e4981a75-3676-4974-8b66-021fbff4fd40")
	)
	(text_box "NOTE 1  THE SENSE IS ITS OWN NET.  /AGND_SENSE has exactly three nodes - U1 pin 3 (-IN), R5's bottom pad, R8 - and R8 (0 ohm) is the ONE tie to GND, at the string bottom.  U1 pin 3 must\n        NEVER carry a GND label or a GND symbol, and no second tie may be added anywhere.  A PART and not a label because a divider passes a ground offset at UNITY while dividing\n        the signal by K = 0.400 (1 mV between string bottom and converter = 2.5 mV at the terminal, half the 25 degC budget), and on a shared GND net the B.Cu pour would tie pin 3\n        to the pour AT THE CONVERTER just as it ties pin 4.  Split, the reading is K*(V_sig - V_S) + Vos - the only residual is the J1-return-to-string-bottom pour offset, at UNITY,\n        carrying just the string's 5 uA: sub-1 uV.  -IN sits ~0.25 uV off U1 GND through R8, six orders inside the -0.3/+0.5 V window.  P7: keep the run dedicated.\nNOTE 2  The guard ring around /AIN_DIV and U3 +IN is P7 COPPER on /AIN_BUF (the buffer OUTPUT), never on /AIN_DIV itself.  No schematic element.\nNOTE 3  R7 + C2 + C8 are the ADS8326's own recommended rail entry (figs 44/45): R7 upstream of both caps, C2 the smaller and closest to the pin.  It isolates U1 ALONE - U2 and U3 stay upstream on +3V3.  No ferrite.\nNOTE 4  NO series resistor between U2 VOUT and C3 / U1 REF (recorded ruling): a SAR's reference current varies with input code, so a series R becomes a code-dependent nonlinearity.\n        C5 >= 1 uF is MANDATORY - the ADR4520's 1-100 uF load-capacitance window is two-ended.\nNOTE 5  R1-R5 are FIVE EQUAL 200 k elements in ONE string tapped 3:2 (K = 0.400, Rtot 1.00 Mohm, tap Thevenin 240 kohm).  Do not collapse.\nNOTE 6  *** J2 MIS-MATE IS DESTRUCTIVE AND UNPROTECTED: pin 1 = +3V3 and pin 6 = GND, so a 180 degree reversal shorts the host's rail to its own ground through the cable.  No series\n        protection, no reverse diode, no keyed housing - all excluded by the scope tier.  P6 must silk a pin-1 marker and a 1..6 legend. ***\nNOTE 7  HOST POWER-UP: wait >= 50 ms after +3V3 before trusting a conversion.  The reference settles in 90 us typ, but slew-limited charging of the ~49.2 uF on VREF at its 10 mA\n        source limit is ALREADY 7-10 ms - a 10 ms wait has ~1x margin; 50 ms restores the 5x it was meant to carry."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
